The instructions you're following are correct, but they're for a different OpenVINO distribution method than what you installed via pip.

Quick Answer
You installed OpenVINO using the PyPI distribution (pip install openvino), which only provides the Python API and doesn't include the setupvars.sh script. The instructions you found are for the Archive distribution downloaded from the OpenVINO release page, which includes the full toolkit with C++ headers, samples, and environment setup scripts.

Detailed Explanation
Two Different Installation Methods
OpenVINO provides multiple distribution channels, each with different contents:

Archive Distribution (what the instructions reference):

Downloaded from release page as a .tgz file
Contains both C/C++ and Python APIs
Includes code samples and C++ headers
Contains setupvars.sh script for environment configuration
Extracted to directories like /opt/intel/openvino_2026.0.0/ install-openvino-archive-linux.rst:10-18
PyPI Distribution (what you installed):

Installed via pip install openvino
Python API only install-openvino-pip.rst:12-17
No setupvars.sh script needed
Environment is automatically configured when used in Python
The setupvars.sh Script
The setupvars.sh script is located in the archive distribution and sets up environment variables for C++ development: setupvars.sh:1-175

It configures:

Library paths (LD_LIBRARY_PATH)
Python paths (PYTHONPATH)
CMake configuration paths
TBB library paths
What You Should Do
For building whisper.cpp with OpenVINO support, you need the Archive distribution because:

whisper.cpp is a C/C++ project that needs OpenVINO's C++ libraries and headers
The build system needs to locate OpenVINO libraries via environment variables set by setupvars.sh
To fix this:

Download the OpenVINO archive package from the release page
Extract it to a directory like /opt/intel/openvino_2026.0.0/
Source the setupvars script: source /opt/intel/openvino_2026.0.0/setupvars.sh
Then build whisper.cpp with OpenVINO support
The pip installation is fine for Python development but insufficient for C++ projects like whisper.cpp.
